--TEST--
`Novis\Image\Image::placeholder` of a plain image gives each `PlaceholderKind` its fixed text, `palette` of it returns its one colour, a transparent image has no palette, and a `count` above 256 throws a `LogicError` — rule:core-classes/image-one-entry-point-per-job
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Novis\Image\Image::placeholder, Novis\Image\Image::palette, Novis\Image\PlaceholderKind
use Novis\Image\Image;
use Novis\Image\Color;
use Novis\Image\PlaceholderKind;

var $plain = Image::create(60, 40, Color::hex("#2050c0"))->encode();

// The characters 3 to 6 of a BlurHash are its average colour, so they are the same for every image of this colour.
echo Image::placeholder($plain, PlaceholderKind::BlurHash), "\n";
echo Image::placeholder($plain, PlaceholderKind::ThumbHash), "\n";

foreach (Image::palette($plain) as Color $colour) {
    echo $colour->r, " ", $colour->g, " ", $colour->b, " ", $colour->alpha, "\n";
}

// Transparent pixels are not counted, so a transparent image has no colours.
var $clear = Image::create(10, 10, Color::rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.0))->encode();
echo Core\Arr::count(Image::palette($clear)), " colours\n";

try {
    Image::palette($plain, 257);
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
L33wY{kbfQkbp3fRfQfRfQfQfQfQ
2aMBBYAPSGyJeHiIh3iHd/SIBql3
32 80 192 1
0 colours
a palette has at most 256 colours, and 257 were asked for
